    "analysis": "<p>React Native's JavaScript Interface (JSI) enables synchronous C++ and JavaScript interop without serialization over the legacy bridge. However, creating custom <code>jsi::HostObject</code> instances that capture JS functions or closures directly inside C++ heap-allocated delegates introduces hidden retain cycles. Because Hermes/V8 garbage collectors cannot traverse C++ <code>std::shared_ptr</code> graphs, instances remain resident indefinitely.</p><p>Furthermore, invoking JavaScript callbacks directly from background native threads without marshalling execution onto the JS thread queue causes race conditions and frame drops (thread jitter), frequently crashing the runtime with <code>EXC_BAD_ACCESS</code> due to concurrent access to the <code>jsi::Runtime</code>.</p>",
